      "writtenOn": "2025-08-26T07:48:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will need to be a lot more detailed to contain all combinations of sampled texture types in WGSL, so something like:\n\n```\nkTexture2D_F32\nkTexture2D_I32\nkTexture2D_U32\nkTextureCube_F32,\n...\n```\n\nThis is because in the generated shader we need to access a different placeholder binding for each of these types.\n\nIt\u0027d be also really nice to have `kNullBinding` that we\u0027ll always keep at offset 0. This means that getting the default binding for a non-kNullBinding will be `myBindingArray[metadata.length - runtimeBindingType]` (we never access kNullBinding bindings because they are empty, but Dawn really wants to have an enum value for it to disable bindings).\n\nSo `binding_type_to_default_index` could instead be `std::vector\u003cRuntimeBindingType\u003e binding_type_order` with a requirement that `kNullBinding` is the first one. Then `binding_type_to_default_index` can be created inside the transform itself.",
      "revId": "afec59677afcd1d32056d81f21b7d1ff5026118a",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
